<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18670" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fōtus</span></b> , ūs,
			m.
		foveo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a warming</i>, <i>fomenting</i> (post-Aug., rare
			except in abl.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Amm. 21, 2,
			3</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">solis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lact. 1, 12, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">decoctum eorum coeliacos juvat et potione et
					fotu,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					23, 1, 10, § 14</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">23, 9, 82,
				§ 164</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fotus ex aqua calida,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cael.
						Aur. Tard. 2, 7, 97</span></i>
			.—In plur., <i><span class="en">Mart.
					Cap. 1, § 35</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">blandis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. Ham. 304</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: queis gloria fotibus aucta Sic cluat,
			Prud. cont. <i><span class="en">Symm. 2, 584</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
